---
import "../../styles/portal.css";
import { ArrowLeft, BadgeCheck, CloudCog, ExternalLink, KeyRound, Rocket } from "@lucide/astro";
import Disclaimer from "../../components/Disclaimer.astro";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Connect Cloudflare DNS to the Ninja Paws Azure deployment." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#101820" />
    <title>Cloudflare setup | PawPrint Portal</title>
  </head>
  <body class="connector-body">
    <Disclaimer />
    <header class="topbar">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Return to PawPrint Portal">
        <img src="/pawprint-mark.svg" alt="" width="36" height="36" />
        <span>Paw<strong>Print</strong> Portal</span>
      </a>
      <span class="connector-optional">Optional connector</span>
      <a class="auth-link" href="/"><ArrowLeft aria-hidden="true" size={16} /> Back</a>
    </header>

    <main class="connector-main">
      <div class="connector-heading">
        <CloudCog aria-hidden="true" size={30} />
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">External DNS / guided setup</p>
          <h1>Cloudflare DNS</h1>
          <p>Connect the <strong>ninjapaws.org</strong> zone without moving application infrastructure out of Azure.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="ownership-band" aria-label="Infrastructure ownership">
        <div><strong>Shared framework</strong><span>Bicep Static Web App module, DNS connector, permission verification</span></div>
        <div><strong>Repository-owned</strong><span>Zone name, custom hostname, GitHub Environment secret</span></div>
        <div><strong>Cloudflare-managed</strong><span>One validation TXT and one DNS-only CNAME</span></div>
      </aside>

      <ol class="connector-steps">
        <li class="connector-step">
          <div class="step-number">1</div>
          <div>
            <h2>Create a seven-day bootstrap token</h2>
            <p>In Cloudflare, select the <strong>Create Account Tokens</strong> template. Keep <strong>Account API Tokens Write</strong>, add <strong>Zone Read</strong>, restrict the zone to <strong>ninjapaws.org</strong>, and set expiry to <strong>7 days</strong>. This temporary token is used once to create the restricted deployment token.</p>
            <button type="button" class="step-action" data-open-cloudflare>Open Cloudflare in Edge <ExternalLink aria-hidden="true" size={16} /></button>
            <a class="provider-fallback" href="https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/api-tokens" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open in this browser instead</a>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="connector-step">
          <div class="step-number">2</div>
          <div>
            <h2>Create, verify, and store the DNS token</h2>
            <p>PawPrint uses the bootstrap token to create a new seven-day account token with only <strong>Zone Read</strong> and <strong>DNS Write</strong> for <strong>ninjapaws.org</strong>, verifies it with a temporary TXT probe, then sends only that new token over stdin to GitHub Environment secrets for Site development and production.</p>
            <form class="guided-token-form" data-cloudflare-form>
              <label for="cloudflare-token"><KeyRound aria-hidden="true" size={16} /> Temporary bootstrap token</label>
              <div>
                <input id="cloudflare-token" name="token" type="password" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" required minlength="20" />
                <button type="submit">Verify and store</button>
              </div>
            </form>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="connector-step">
          <div class="step-number">3</div>
          <div>
            <h2>Confirm connection</h2>
            <dl class="guided-status" data-cloudflare-status>
              <div><dt>Development</dt><dd>Checking</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Production</dt><dd>Checking</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Token expiry</dt><dd>Checking</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Deployment workflow</dt><dd>Checking</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <p class="guided-message" data-cloudflare-message aria-live="polite">No token is retained by this browser or written to disk. After successful setup, revoke the bootstrap token in Cloudflare; PawPrint never stores it.</p>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="connector-step">
          <div class="step-number">4</div>
          <div>
            <h2>Deploy and bind</h2>
            <p>The Site workflow deploys Azure with Bicep, reconciles the two Cloudflare records, then converges the Azure custom-domain resource through Bicep before publishing the application. Review and push the workflow changes to the <strong>dev</strong> branch first; the button remains disabled until both the workflow and token are ready.</p>
            <button type="button" class="step-action deploy-action" data-cloudflare-deploy disabled><Rocket aria-hidden="true" size={16} /> Deploy Site</button>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="connector-result" data-connector-result hidden>
        <BadgeCheck aria-hidden="true" size={20} />
        <span></span>
      </div>
    </main>
    <script is:inline src="/cloudflare-setup.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>